<!-- Full Dashboard Card Exercise (Words)
1. Dashboard Container

Make a parent full-width section.

Add max width for very large screens.

Center the container horizontally.

Add padding on all sides.

2. Grid Layout

Turn the container into a grid.

Add gap between items.

Responsive columns:

Small screens → 1 column

Medium screens → 2 columns

Large screens → 3 columns

3. Card Container

Each grid item is a card.

Card should have:

Rounded corners

Shadow

White background

Overflow hidden

Padding inside

Hover effect to scale slightly

4. Card Content

Top of the card: image

Full width of the card

Fixed height

Object-fit so it crops nicely

Below the image: text content

Title → bold, noticeable

Subtitle → smaller, muted

Paragraph → description

Bottom of the card: button

Rounded

Background color

Hover effect

5. Responsive Behavior

Cards resize automatically with screen width.

Text and buttons remain readable.

Grid columns adjust based on breakpoints.

💡 How to think in Tailwind while writing HTML:

Start with container → grid → cards

Decide how many columns at each screen size

Add gap between cards

Style each card individually with rounded corners, shadow, and overflow

Add image + content + button inside the card -->